From: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: own virtual port redirects and RX teardown

Drive the uplink inject. The previous patch added the primitive that tags a
received frame with a virtual port as its source and pushes it into the
PPE; this hooks the wireless receive path so real packets reach it,
completing the wireless-to-wired offload.

Complete the virtual-port datapath transaction with source-VP-aware scatter
assembly, an unexpected-punt circuit breaker, and teardown ordering which
quiesces ingress callbacks before physical EDMA carriers disappear.

Merged from:
  0520-01-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-intercept-virtual-port-uplink.patch
  0520-02-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-harden-virtual-port-rx-and-teardown.patch

Based on work by:
  Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>

Signed-off-by: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

